\par}}}}\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li5028\ri501\sl235\slmult1\f6\fs22\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 a curvature plot is often drawn. A curvature plot means that in a large number of points of a curve the curvature is calculated and plotted perpendicular to the curve ( the purple line). Since the curvature can be positive as well as negative, the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 plot can\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 swap\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 from one\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 side\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 of the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 curve\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the other (see the image left). Where the plot intersects the curve the curvature is zero. So in areas of a curve where the curvature is zero (straight line segments), both curves are on top of each other. At a knuckle point on the other hand\par\sect\sectd\sbknone\cols2\colno1\colw1612\colsr3026\colno2\colw5846\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li390\sl240\slmult1\sb136\f5\fs20\b0\i1\expnd0\expndtw-2\charscalex100 Illustration\expnd2\expndtw10  \expnd-1\expndtw-5 30\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li390\ri505\sl232\slmult1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 \column \f6\fs22 the\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 curvature is\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 very\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 high\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 and\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 can\expnd-1\expndtw-4  \expnd0\expndtw0 go\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 infinity.\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 So the higher the absolute value of the curvature, the\par\sect\sectd\sbknone\cols1\colno1\colw10484\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li284\ri419\sl235\slmult1\f6\fs22\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 further the curvature plot is drawn away from the curve. Smooth curves are characterized by curvature plots\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 with\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 no\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 unexpected\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 humps or\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 hollows,\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 curvature must change gradually\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 as\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 is\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the case with the waterline below. The scale of the curvature plot can be decreased {\*\bkmkstart _bookmark52}{\*\bkmkend _bookmark52}by pressing the F9 key and increased by pressing the F10 key. Make sure that the {\field {\fldinst { HYPERLINK \\l "bookmark52" }}{\fldrslt \cf3{\ul curvature visibility}}
